\ `add2` has no row, so it takes the whole stack. A value pushed earlier is
\ still on the stack under its inputs, unlike a local that is still to be
\ used, so the call is refused.
: add2 ( a:Int^many b:Int^many -- r:Int^many ) prim + ;

: value-below
  ( x:Int^many n:Int^many -- r:Int^many s:Int^many )
  locals { x n } { n x 1 add2 };
